4. Entity Relationship Explanation
USERS → STUDENTS
USERS 1 ───────── 0..1 STUDENTS

A user account can be associated with one student profile.

students.user_id references users.id.

STUDENTS → ENROLLMENTS
STUDENTS 1 ───────── N ENROLLMENTS

One student can have multiple course enrollments.

students.id
     ↓
enrollments.student_id

COURSES → ENROLLMENTS
COURSES 1 ───────── N ENROLLMENTS

One course can have many enrolled students.

The enrollments table therefore works as the junction table between students and courses.

STUDENTS N ─────── N COURSES
              │
              │
        ENROLLMENTS

STUDENTS → ATTENDANCE
STUDENTS 1 ───────── N ATTENDANCE

A student can have many attendance records.

Example:

Student 101
    │
    ├── 2026-09-01 → Present
    ├── 2026-09-02 → Present
    ├── 2026-09-03 → Absent
    └── 2026-09-04 → Present

STUDENTS → MARKS
STUDENTS 1 ───────── N MARKS

A student can have marks for multiple courses.

Example:

Student
   │
   ├── Mathematics → 85
   ├── Science     → 90
   └── English     → 78

COURSES → MARKS
COURSES 1 ───────── N MARKS

A course can have marks belonging to many students.

